========================================================================================
TAKEAWAY
========================================================================================
  1. The via-max alpha=2/7 density floor is exactly the wrong target:
     explicit admissible anti-correlation cases have rho_{2/7}=0.
  2. The global alpha=1/7 object is much fatter in every case scanned;
     this is the correct reservoir for a direct LRC witness.
  3. The critical-gap scan suggests a stronger open subtarget:
     prove a uniform critical slack sup_{x in G_P} maxgap(E*x) >= beta
     with beta>1/7, and then separately prove a density floor below beta.
     The tested anti-correlations bind only at the via boundary, not at
     the global threshold.
  4. This does not prove LRC(14).  It moves the proof target from
     'rho*>=c0' to the precise two-part statement: global/slack reservoir
     plus Weyl/CRT placement cannot be fully covered by conditional blockers.
